n from tenets of his plan, especially help for seniors and the unemployed.  [McCAIN&nbsp- says retirees need relief; speaks about what the people are being asked; states we cannot spend the next four years waiting for our luck to change.]  [In Ohio, OBAMA&nbsp- comments on capital gains.] ", "segment_duration": 290, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907964, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "7MVd4V960t", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-14", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1740, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907963, "segment_id": "NRt6dhClkm", "segment_broadcast_id": "7MVd4V960t", "segment_title": "Economy: Bank Rescue Plan", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric)  President Bush's announcement that a stake will be bought in big banks to encourage lending noted.  Stock Market Report.  \n\n(New York: Anthony Mason)  The plan that will make taxpayers shareholders in the banks featured; details given about how some of the billions will be used in the nine biggest banks and the guarantee of loans.  [Treasury Secretary Henry PAULSON\u00a0- says we must restore confidence in our system.]  [BUSH\u00a0- says banks can make loans now.]  [Princeton University economist Paul KRUGMAN\u2020- says no one is sure it will work.]  [High Frequency Economics Carl WEINBERG\u2020- says the plan will not keep us out of a recession.]  The announcement of jobs cuts by PepsiCo noted. ", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63340.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907965, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_w