"YJf3L2XmoU", "segment_broadcast_id": "7MVd4V960t", "segment_title": "Where They Stand (HIV/AIDS)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric)  Statistics on HIV/AIDS in America cited  \n\n(Washington: Sanjay Gupta)  Where presidential candidates Senators Barack Obama and John McCain stand on the issue of HIV/AIDS in the US featured; details recalled of President Bush's plans for global AIDS relief.  [Black AIDS Inst. founder Phill WILSON&#134;- comments on the Bush legacy, the irony of neglecting the domestic epidemic and the apathy in the community about AIDS.]  Statistics on AIDS among blacks and the incidence of AIDS in Washington, DC, cited.  [CDC director Julie GERBERDING&nbsp- comments on the shame and ignorance re: AIDS.]  [HIV-positive \"RUSSELL\", \"DANIELLE\"&nbsp- comment on AIDS, their health care and the candidates' plans.]  [OBAMA&nbsp- says we need a more effective AIDS policy.]  The plans from Obama and McCain for handling AIDS and how each plan would work for those like Russell and Danielle outlined.  [McCAIN&nbsp- says we need a domestic plan.]  \n\n(Studio: Katie Couric)  Tomorrow's series on Presidential Questions previewed. ", "segment_duration": 390, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63800.0", "legacy_segment_id": 907970, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "7MVd4V960t", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-14", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1740, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 907963, "segment_id": "dwZL1Ky5E6", "segment_broadcast_id": "7MVd4V960t", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Campbell's Soup; Smart Start; Advair; Obama's ad; Hunt's.)", "segment_description": " ", "segment_duration": 150, "segm